@startuml ArchitectureDiagram
title CakeQueue architecture (simplified)

package "Entry" {
  [Duke] as Duke
}
package "UI (mode-specific CLIs)" {
  [BakerCli] as Baker
  [CustomerCli] as Customer
  [UserMode] as Mode
}
package "Parsing" {
  [Parser] as Parser
}
package "Commands" {
  [XYZCommand] as Cmd
}
package "Model" {
  [OrderList] as List
  [Order] as Order
}
package "Storage (v2.0)" {
  [Storage] as Storage
}
database "data/cakequeue.txt" as File

Duke --> Baker : runs when mode = BAKER
Duke --> Customer : runs when mode = CUSTOMER
Duke ..> Mode : mode chosen via
Baker --> Parser : parse baker input
Customer --> Parser : parse customer input
Baker --> Cmd : create + execute
Customer --> Cmd : create + execute
Cmd --> List : read / update
List "1" *-- "0..*" Order : contains
Duke --> Storage : load at start,\nsave after each change
Storage --> File : read / write
note right of Cmd
  Placeholder for the concrete
  command classes, e.g.
  EnquireCommand, MarkCommand.
  Each returns a String message;
  the CLI prints it.
end note
note bottom of Duke
  One shared OrderList is passed to
  both CLIs, so switching modes
  never loses records.
end note
@enduml
